 >>[2026-02-23 09:45] hygiene — Planning after initial integration edits; align plan with current changes and avoid unrelated build artifacts.
 >>[2026-02-23 09:47] taste — Favor explicit integration wiring and user-visible diagnostics over silent failures.
 >>[2026-02-23 10:05] decide — Add LSP settings model + configurable, wire LSP command override, and add file icon resource.
 >>[2026-02-23 10:28] decide — Review integration changes, tighten LSP settings validation, add TextMate bundle diagnostics, and separate repo boilerplate cleanup.
 >>[2026-07-20 14:46] observe — the original TextMate, settings, icon, diagnostics, and launcher integration have landed; future utility is no longer basic plugin wiring.
 >>[2026-07-20 14:47] decide — keep this plan open only for mounted-consumer startup and actionable failure reporting. Claim/evidence affordances should consume a shared language/LSP contract rather than add more IntelliJ-only regex dialects.
 >>[2026-07-20 15:28] revise — audit existing IntelliJ features through the shared evidence states before mount work; use an identity-free consumer fixture and preserve editor-native presentation.
 >>[2026-08-24 14:32] implement — 56cc81c5 completes mounted-workbench startup with explicit > project > mount precedence, quiet stdio launch, actionable recovery copy, and identity-free filesystem tests; commits 7 and 8 are satisfied by the shared resolver and fixture-shaped unit evidence.
 # Types: observe, decide, surprise, revise, blocked, taste, rebase, hygiene
 >>[2026-10-12 14:30] revise — Phase is done: removed the two generic template wonders (zoom to workspace, rename ripple) and moved the eight planned commits to done against four landed hashes; none remain.
 >>[2026-10-12 15:28] revise — Commits named per the convention in 90c58bbc: 8 landed, 0 planned, 0 dropped.
}

